# Nightshift — master env schema. NAMES ONLY. NEVER VALUES.
#
# Doppler holds every value. This file exists so a new variable has one
# place to be declared and reviewed in git before it gets a value.
#
# SCOPE: only environments that have no repo of their own. Today that means
# the managed-platform install (.builder), which is not a git repo and so has no .env.example
# of its own. Target repos keep theirs — never copy a target repo's vars in
# here, or the two drift and the stale copy wins silently.
#
# Adding a variable: append the name with an empty value, commit, then set
# the value in Doppler (dev config). Never paste a value into this file.

# --- managed platform (.builder) ---
